message: "If you use or adapt this curriculum, please cite it as below."
title: "The AI Starter Kit: A curriculum for people who hate AI or think it's too complicated"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "somehippie"
repository-code: "https://github.com/somehippie/ai-starter-kit-digital-tasks"
url: "https://github.com/somehippie/ai-starter-kit-digital-tasks"
abstract: >-
  An eight-session, research-grounded AI-literacy curriculum for two
  audiences — AI skeptics and AI beginners — with distinct entry ramps
  that converge by session two. Prioritizes verification and calibration
  before productivity, and includes a "doom loop" field guide covering
  failure modes such as sycophancy, cognitive debt, and AI-enabled
  impersonation scams.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - AI literacy
  - digital literacy
  - curriculum
  - education
  - adult education
  - media literacy
